# chip — occurrence-ALIGNED placement twin of chip_topdown (study fixture,
# NOT in the QoR corpus): built with build_hier_demo's --align-occurrences,
# which snaps same-cell instances onto shared rows/columns after SA so their
# congruent block edges COINCIDE in the flat Hanan grid (2/3 of each cell
# class aligned here; the third would overlap).  Hanan crossings drop 33%
# (242x262=63404 -> 227x187=42449).  Study verdict (2026-07-31, planner 2x2
# matrix in flow/chip/ReadMe.md): the grid reduction paid on the OLD
# copy-dominated planner (374.5 -> 300.5s) but is a wash after the undo-log/
# cut-index/leaf-cache fixes (~110 -> ~120s) — the remaining cost is
# congestion-driven, and the snap costs QoR (unplaced 3341 -> 3877: it closes
# part of the SA bloat channels).  Kept as the test-with-both twin.
source chip_tracks.buda
open_bdb chip_aligned.bdb.sql
derive_busterms 2
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip
add_blocks_from_bdb 2 skip
set_max_bundle_bits auto
run_hier_bundler depth 2
generate_hier_topologies
set_planner_param healersAhead 1
run_planner hier 5 signal_tracks
run_nuts
run_detailed_nuts
negotiate_congestion
report_wl
check_design
exit
